      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are a few options, depending on the tone you prefer for your handbook.\n\n**Option 1 (Inclusive and Direct):**\n\n\"We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful environment for all team members, and this includes the respectful use of preferred pronouns. We understand that some may view this as a necessary step in recognizing and supporting the diverse gender identities of our staff, while others might see it as a more evolving social standard. Our policy supports the right of every individual to be addressed in a way that affirms their identity here at the company, promoting a foundation of respect for all in the workplace.\n\n**Option 2 (More Neutral and Policy-Focused):**\n\n\"In the interest of promoting a supportive and professional workplace, we are adopting a policy that supports the use of preferred pronouns for all employees. This approach is rooted in the belief that respect is fundamental to a positive work culture, though we acknowledge that views on this topic vary widely among the community. We ask that all team members respect the pronouns that their colleagues choose to use, as this is a key part of our commitment to professional and unbiased interaction.\n\n**Option \n\n**\n\nChoose the one that best aligns with your company's overall culture and legal",
